<article class="env-proposition" id="BDE7B0">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/BDE7B0">Proposition <span data-tag="BDE7B0">4.1.2.12</span>.</a> Suppose given a commutative diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { X \ar [r]^{i} \ar [dr]^{p} \ar [d] &amp;  X' \ar [d]^{p'} \\ X'' \ar [r]^{p''} &amp;  S } \]
</div>
  <p> of simplicial sets. Assume that $i$ is a cofibration, and that $p,p'$, and $p''$ are smooth. Then the induced map $X' \coprod _{X} X'' \rightarrow S$ is smooth. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows immediately from Corollary <a href="/tag/157BCE" data-tag="157BCE">4.1.2.3</a> and characterization $(1)$ of Proposition <a href="/tag/876ECD" data-tag="876ECD">4.1.2.7</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>